    <sec sec-type="nigel-editorial-summary" specific-use="nigel-envelope" id="EC0">
      <title>Editorial summary</title>
      <p specific-use="nigel-empty" content-type="not-applicable" id="EC0.p001" />
    </sec>
    <sec id="sec1" sec-type="intro">
      <title>Introduction</title>
      <p id="p_1_1" specific-use="nigel-labelable">Fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) restores the gut community.<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref1">1</xref>,<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref2">2</xref> It is
        used for <italic>C difficile</italic> infection (CDI) with <bold>high</bold> cure rates.</p>
      <p id="p_1_2">Colony counts reach 10<sup>9</sup> CFU/g; H<sub>2</sub>O is the diluent (<xref ref-type="table" rid="tbl1">Table 1</xref>, <xref ref-type="fig" rid="fig1">Figure 1</xref>).</p>
    </sec>
    <sec id="sec2">
      <title>Methods</title>
      <sec id="sec2.1">
        <title>Statistical Analysis</title>
        <p id="p_2_1">Cure rate was modelled as <inline-formula><tex-math>p = \frac{k}{n}</tex-math></inline-formula> and pooled by</p>
        <disp-formula id="eq1"><tex-math>\hat{p} = \frac{\sum k_i}{\sum n_i}</tex-math></disp-formula>
        <p id="p_2_2">with a random-effects model.<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref3">3</xref></p>
      </sec>
      <table-wrap id="tbl1">
        <label>Table 1</label>
